# What a service gets by depending on platform-common, without knowing this module's packages.
#
# This file is the fix for the failure the module split would otherwise have introduced: these
# classes sit outside every service's @ComponentScan root, and a @Configuration that scanning does
# not find produces no error -- only absent beans. Boot reads this file from every jar on the
# classpath, so adding the dependency is what wires them (ADR-0017).
#
# Order is not significant here; Boot orders auto-configurations by their own @AutoConfiguration
# before/after declarations.
com.xenopsoftware.common.config.AsyncConfiguration
com.xenopsoftware.common.config.JacksonConfiguration
com.xenopsoftware.common.config.LoggingAspectConfiguration
com.xenopsoftware.common.config.LoggingConfiguration
com.xenopsoftware.common.outbox.NatsConnectionConfiguration
com.xenopsoftware.common.outbox.OutboxAutoConfiguration
com.xenopsoftware.common.storage.StorageConfiguration
